Downloading the Software, the public availability of its source code, or the
absence of a fee does not constitute commercial authorization.

A commercial purpose is a purpose primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage, business operations, monetary compensation or revenue
generation. This includes:
- selling, licensing, renting or charging for access to the Software or
  modified versions;
- using the Software in business operations, professional work, paid services,
  or revenue-generating services, including internal business use;
- bundling or integrating the Software into commercial products or services.

A commercial activity remains commercial even when the Software itself is
provided free of charge. Nonprofit, educational, charitable and government
organizations have no blanket exemption: their noncommercial activities are
permitted under section 2, and their commercial activities require authorization.

Commercial authorization may specify its own scope, fees and conditions.
Request it through https://github.com/kkbbzjh/LoliaBloom/issues or another contact
channel explicitly designated by the copyright holder. Do not include passwords,
tokens or other confidential information in public requests.

